The camera wearer is approaching an outdoor food-preparation area. Several volunteers are gathered roughly 2–6 meters ahead, mostly seated or facing the central tables. One person stands very close on the right—about an arm’s length away—facing left toward the work surface, but does not block the wearer’s forward path. Containers and preparation supplies are within reach in the foreground, while no clear vegetables, blender, or plated meals are visible.

Given the group setting and multiple available volunteers, the most socially appropriate next action is to organize assistance with food preparation. This promotes effective teamwork and efficient use of the people and resources present.

